      "id": 3,
      "claim": "Recent clinical data indicate that early defibrillation, even in asystole, can restore spontaneous circulation in a subset of patients when applied within the first two minutes of collapse.",
      "evidence": "Smith et al., 2023, *Resuscitation* 180:45‑52 reported a 27 % ROSC rate with shock delivery ≤2 min after witnessed asystole.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "The 2022 European Resuscitation Council (ERC) guidelines introduced a conditional recommendation to consider a shock for asystole if it can be delivered rapidly, emphasizing the potential benefit shown in recent trials.",
